= Prussia Votes

On 20 February Prussia, two thirds of Germany, elects its Landtag. It is the first real test of the [+ e21_party +]. The campaign is short and cold. Our speakers are shouted down in the Catholic Rhineland and cheered in the Mansfeld copper towns.

[? if kapp_outcome = 3 : The workers' government in Berlin has not touched Prussia, where Otto Braun's ministers and the old officials still rule. ?]

What should the campaign be about?

- @bread: Bread, wages and the price of coal.
- @soviets: Soviet Russia and the councils.
- @tribune: Parliament as a tribune: say what no one else will.

@bread
subtitle: The Right's campaign. Wins votes among the unorganised.
on-arrival: worker_support += 3; unionist_satisfaction += 4; lean_unionist += 1
go-to: result

@soviets
subtitle: The Left's campaign. Fires up the party, frightens the voters.
on-arrival: militancy += 3; worker_support += 1; offensive_satisfaction += 4; lean_offensive += 1
go-to: result

@tribune
subtitle: The Spartacist campaign: use the Landtag to expose, not to govern.
on-arrival: worker_support += 2; luxemburgist_satisfaction += 4; lean_luxemburgist += 1
go-to: result

@result
